                <pb facs="0294" n="158" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg158"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15a3/78a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-24T17:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1929—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>189. President and I are most anxious to have a check-up on accuracy of our
                    figures regarding British cruiser strength as contained in Department’s telegram
                    No. 182, July 21, 7 p.m., before you confer with Gibson and MacDonald on Monday.
                    We find it difficult to make any suggestions or plans until this matter has been
                    cleared up.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
